... speaking of which, this is one of the things that annoys me the most in
nethack. Being made Hand of Elbereth should not penalize the player in this
manner. There should be some way of letting shopkeepers know that you're at the
door - for instance, a #speak command, or making shopkeepers see invisible, or
maybe the first time you bump into a shopkeeper when you're invisible, the
shopkeeper, instead of getting angry, will say "Huh? What? OH! Welcome to
Asidonhopo's little shop of horrors, whoever you are."

As the game stands (2.3), it's easy enough to just deliberately refrain from
getting Hand of Elbereth until you're below all the shops or at least have no
more use for them or have teleport control and so are able to get in that way.
(By the way, what is the maximum depth for shops?) However, if in future
versions, as i have heard, it will be more difficult to gain favor with the
gods, then when one *does* get Hand of Elbereth, it should definitely not be
accompanied by negative effects.

IMHO, anyway.

